	(text_box "DESIGN NOTE D1:\nPorts only: no parts yet. One SPI bus from the FPGA crosses the barrier: SCLK, MOSI and the two chip selects (DAC, ADC) go FPGA -> isolated side, MISO comes back. Left side is FPGA ground (J3), right side is the analog ground of the DAC/ADC. Part selection decides: digital isolator (4 or 6 channels) vs. isolator with built-in isolated supply, and where the isolated rail for the converters comes from (U32 A1212S has its COM tied to GND today). ENABLE crosses here too (ISO_ENABLE drives the PhotoMOS on [8]); spare channels for the safety-logic GPIO come later. Side 1 is powered from +3V3_FPGA / GND_FPGA on J3 [5] (decision pending: ICD_J3 said no power on J3). Six channels: five FPGA -> board, MISO back. Rev 1 fallback: 0 Ohm links in place of the isolator, which makes GND_FPGA = GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
